<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="45–55 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Animals</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Identify common animals with <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">an</span>, choose accurate plural forms, and match singular or plural subjects with <span class="ex">is</span> or <span class="ex">are</span>. Describe a pet, farm animal, or wild animal from a real, pictured, or invented context without guessing from one feature alone.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">45–55 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">articles, plurals, and agreement</span>
    <span class="tag">pets · farm animals · wildlife</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min optional practice</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>One animal or two? Listen to is and are.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Regular, unchanged, and irregular animal plurals.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match, choose, read, and build chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Identify and describe animals from clear evidence.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Regular countable animal words use a singular after <span class="ex">one</span> and a plural after zero or a number greater than one: <span class="ex">one dog · zero dogs · two dogs</span>. Some animal plurals add <span class="ex">-es</span>, some do not change, and some are irregular.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved an from the vowel sound in elephant, cats after two, and are with the plural subject the dogs.">
    <h3>Bring articles, plurals, and <em>be</em> into an animal description</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use earlier lessons. Complete each sentence, then read it aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier grammar choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a">a</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an">an</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cat">cat</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cats">cats</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The photograph shows <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-hint="Elephant begins with a vowel sound, so choose an." data-fix="The photograph shows an elephant." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> elephant.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The shelter profile lists two <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="cats" data-hint="Two requires the regular plural noun cats." data-fix="The shelter profile lists two cats." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The two dogs <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="The subject the two dogs is plural, so use are." data-fix="The two dogs are friendly with their handler." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> friendly with their handler.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the animals</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>These are representative pictures with visible labels. Point to a picture, describe its position, or say the label with <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">an</span>. The label gives the intended answer, so this is language practice rather than a biology test.</p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cat.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a cat</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/dog.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a dog</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bird.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a bird</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/fish.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a fish</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/rabbit.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a rabbit</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/pig.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a pig</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cow.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a cow</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/elephant.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">an elephant</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/horse.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a horse</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/sheep.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a sheep</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/duck.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a duck</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/monkey.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a monkey</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/lion.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a lion</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/tiger.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a tiger</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bear.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a bear</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/owl.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">an owl</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/frog.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a frog</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/snake.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a snake</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/turtle.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a turtle</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/penguin.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a penguin</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/chicken.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a chicken</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/fox.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a fox</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/panda.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a panda</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/giraffe.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a giraffe</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/zebra.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a zebra</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/octopus.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">an octopus</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/dolphin.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a dolphin</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/koala.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a koala</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/kangaroo.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a kangaroo</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/crocodile.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">a crocodile</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>One animal or two?</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">I have a dog. My dog is big.</span><br /><span class="ex">My neighbor has two cats. The cats are small.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <strong>dog</strong> and <strong>cats</strong>. What is at the end of <strong>cats</strong>?</li>
      <li>After <strong>my dog</strong> we say <span class="ex">is</span>. After <strong>the cats</strong> we say a different word. Which word?</li>
      <li>Say these aloud: <span class="ex">a cat, a dog, an elephant, an owl</span>. When do we say <span class="ex">an</span> instead of <span class="ex">a</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You used a or an before one animal and matched is or are to the singular or plural subject.">
    <h3>Discovery check: one or many?</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Say the sentence aloud first. One animal takes a / an and is. Many animals take -s and are.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a">a</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an">an</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a" data-hint="Dog begins with the consonant sound d, so use a." data-fix="I have a dog." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> dog. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(first sound: d)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>In the wildlife center photograph, I see <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-hint="Elephant begins with a vowel sound, so use an." data-fix="In the wildlife center photograph, I see an elephant." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> elephant. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(first sound: e)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The cat <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="The cat names one animal, so use is." data-fix="The cat is black." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> black. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one cat)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The two dogs <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="The two dogs is a plural subject, so use are." data-fix="The two dogs are friendly with their handler." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> friendly with their handler.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>In the tree there is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-hint="Owl begins with a vowel sound, so use an." data-fix="In the tree there is an owl." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> owl. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(first sound: o)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="They and horses are plural, so use are." data-fix="They are horses." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> horses. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(many horses)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: name the animal, count the animal</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Each animal word is a <strong>noun</strong>. Two core patterns work for most animals. A few words use plural rules you learned earlier, and a few do not change.</p>
  <p><strong>1. One animal?</strong> &nbsp;Use <span class="ex">a</span> before a consonant sound, <span class="ex">an</span> before a vowel sound, and say <span class="ex">is</span>: <span class="ex">a dog · an elephant · The dog is big.</span></p>
  <p><strong>2. Zero or more than one?</strong> &nbsp;Drop <span class="ex">a / an</span> and use a plural form after zero or a number greater than one: <span class="ex">zero dogs · two dogs</span>. A plural subject takes <span class="ex">are</span>: <span class="ex">The dogs are big.</span> Most animal words add <span class="ex">-s</span>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>one (singular)</th><th>zero or more than one (plural)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>a</b> dog &nbsp;·&nbsp; the dog <b>is</b> big</td><td>two <b>dogs</b> &nbsp;·&nbsp; the dogs <b>are</b> big</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>a</b> cat &nbsp;·&nbsp; the cat <b>is</b> small</td><td>three <b>cats</b> &nbsp;·&nbsp; the cats <b>are</b> small</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>an</b> owl &nbsp;·&nbsp; it <b>is</b> an owl</td><td>two <b>owls</b> &nbsp;·&nbsp; they <b>are</b> owls</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>a</b> horse · <b>a</b> fox</td><td>two <b>horses</b> · two <b>foxes</b> <span class="contraction">(add -es)</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>a</b> sheep · <b>a</b> fish</td><td>two <b>sheep</b> · two <b>fish</b> <span class="contraction">(commonly no change)</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>a</b> mouse · <b>an</b> octopus</td><td>two <b>mice</b> · two <b>octopuses</b> <span class="contraction">(special forms)</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Pet, farm animal, wild animal, or wildlife?</h3>
    <p>These labels describe an animal's relationship with people and its situation, not a fixed biological group.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A <strong>pet</strong> lives with a person mainly for companionship.</li>
      <li>A <strong>farm animal</strong> is kept or raised on a farm.</li>
      <li>A <strong>wild animal</strong> lives independently in nature. The group word <strong>wildlife</strong> is uncountable: <span class="ex">We saw wildlife</span>, not <span class="ex">a wildlife</span>.</li>
      <li>Context matters. A rabbit can be a pet, a farm animal, or a wild animal.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Observe unknown wildlife from a safe distance. Do not approach, feed, or handle it. Follow local signs and expert guidance.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: the plural <span class="ex">-s</span> has three sounds</h3>
    <p>The spelling is usually <span class="ex">-s</span>, but the final sound follows the animal word before it. Listen to the ending; it helps you hear one animal or many.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>ending sound</th><th>examples</th><th>what you hear</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>“s”</td><td><span class="ex">cat<strong>s</strong> · rabbit<strong>s</strong></span></td><td>a quiet air sound</td></tr>
        <tr><td>“z”</td><td><span class="ex">dog<strong>s</strong> · bird<strong>s</strong> · owl<strong>s</strong></span></td><td>a voiced, buzzing sound</td></tr>
        <tr><td>“iz”</td><td><span class="ex">horse<strong>s</strong> · fox<strong>es</strong></span></td><td>one extra spoken syllable</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Longer animal words also have one strong beat: <span class="ex"><strong>AN</strong>-i-mal · <strong>EL</strong>-e-phant · gi-<strong>RAFFE</strong> · <strong>RAB</strong>-bit · <strong>CHICK</strong>-en · <strong>PEN</strong>-guin</span>. Say the full noun chunk: <span class="ex">an <strong>EL</strong>ephant · two <strong>HORS</strong>es</span>.</p>
    <p>In common U.S. English, <span class="ex">zebra</span> often begins like <span class="ex">zee</span>: <span class="ex"><strong>ZEE</strong>-bruh</span>. Other English varieties may begin it like <span class="ex">zeb</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Can we say <span class="ex">the dogs is big</span>? <strong>No.</strong> Two dogs are many, so we say <span class="ex">the dogs are big</span>.</li>
      <li>Can we say <span class="ex">two cat</span>? <strong>No.</strong> After <span class="ex">two</span> we need the plural: <span class="ex">two cats</span>.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Sheep</span> does not change: <span class="ex">one sheep, two sheep</span>. The usual plural of <span class="ex">fish</span> is also <span class="ex">fish</span>: <span class="ex">one fish, two fish</span>. In scientific or specialized contexts, <span class="ex">fishes</span> can mean different species or types of fish.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">A chicken</span> means one animal. Uncountable <span class="ex">chicken</span> can also mean the meat: <span class="ex">We ate chicken.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read singular and plural animal listening check">
    <h2>Listen: one animal or more?</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Your teacher reads each numbered sentence once at a natural speed and once more slowly. Listen before you choose.</p>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You heard the singular and plural noun forms, the article an before owl, and the animal named in each complete sentence.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening check</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Listening choices">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cat">cat</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cats">cats</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="dog">dog</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="dogs">dogs</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="horse">horse</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="horses">horses</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sheep">sheep</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sheeps">sheeps</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a">a</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an">an</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="zebra">zebra</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="giraffe">giraffe</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The photo shows one <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="cat" data-hint="Listen for the noun without a final s after one." data-fix="The photo shows one cat." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The shelter has two <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="dogs" data-hint="Listen for the z sound at the end of dogs after two." data-fix="The shelter has two dogs." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>There are three <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="horses" data-hint="Listen for the extra syllable at the end of horses." data-fix="There are three horses near the fence." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button> near the fence.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The field has two <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sheep" data-hint="Sheep has the same form for one animal and more than one." data-fix="The field has two sheep." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>There is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-hint="Listen for an before the vowel sound in owl." data-fix="There is an owl in the tree." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button> owl in the tree.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>In the photo, I see a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="zebra" data-hint="Listen for ZEE-bruh in common U.S. pronunciation." data-fix="In the photo, I see a zebra." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>Teacher: open the script after the learner checks</summary>
      <ol><li>The photo shows one cat.</li><li>The shelter has two dogs.</li><li>There are three horses near the fence.</li><li>The field has two sheep.</li><li>There is an owl in the tree.</li><li>In the photo, I see a zebra.</li></ol>
    </details>
  </section>

  <h2>Animal words in real chunks</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>People talk about animals in short chunks. Keep these together:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">I have a dog. &nbsp; · &nbsp; I don’t have a pet. &nbsp; · &nbsp; I like cats.</span><br /><span class="ex">It’s a cat. &nbsp; · &nbsp; It is small and black. &nbsp; · &nbsp; They are friendly.</span></p>
  <p>And chunks about other people: <span class="ex">My neighbor has two dogs. &nbsp; · &nbsp; My friend has a bird.</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Each clue uses a specific visible feature, sound, behavior, or relationship that identifies one answer in this lesson.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the animal from the clue</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the clue, then choose the animal that fits</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="dog">dog</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cat">cat</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="horse">horse</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fish">fish</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sheep">sheep</button>
