        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It is a rabbit.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> I have a dog. &nbsp;→&nbsp; make it two</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I have two dogs.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to share information about your home, street, or a real pet. Choose a labeled picture, a public place, or an invented animal profile. Observe unknown animals from a safe distance rather than approaching or handling them.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A pictured or invented pet:</b> Choose a lesson picture or invent a profile. Say <span class="ex">This is a cat. She is small and gray.</span> You can also say <span class="ex">I don't have a pet, but I like dogs.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A city wildlife report:</b> Use a public photograph or an invented city. Name and count three animals with <span class="ex">a</span>, <span class="ex">an</span>, or a plural: <span class="ex">There is an owl. There are two foxes.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Categories in context:</b> Choose a rabbit, cat, chicken, or another animal. Explain whether it is a pet, farm animal, or wild animal in your chosen situation. Change the situation and see whether the category changes.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A safe observation:</b> Describe an animal from a picture or a safe distance. Say what you can observe, not what you assume: <span class="ex">It is brown. It has four legs. It is near a tree.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Information gap:</b> Describe a labeled animal in short sentences and keep adding observable clues until only one answer is clear. Your teacher guesses, then you change roles. <span class="ex">It is a bird. It is black and white. It swims, but it cannot fly.</span></div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: an animal information card</h3>
    <p>Create a short card for an animal shelter, farm visit, or wildlife center. Use a real public example, a lesson picture, or an invented profile.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Name one animal with the correct article: <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">an</span>.</li>
      <li>Add one accurate singular or plural sentence with <span class="ex">is</span> or <span class="ex">are</span>.</li>
      <li>Give a pet, farm animal, or wild animal category and explain the context.</li>
      <li>Give at least three observable features without guessing personality or behavior.</li>
      <li>Add one respectful or safe action for a visitor.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Present the card for 30 to 45 seconds. Then answer one follow-up question from your teacher.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For one animal I say <strong>a</strong> or <strong>an</strong> and use <strong>is</strong>: <span class="ex">the cat ___ small</span>. After zero or a number greater than one, I use a plural form: <span class="ex">zero cats · two cats</span>. A plural subject uses ______: <span class="ex">the dogs ___ big</span>.”</p>
    <p>Name one plural that adds <span class="ex">-s</span> or <span class="ex">-es</span>, one that does not change, and one irregular plural. Then explain why one animal, such as a rabbit, can fit different categories in different contexts. You may use an invented example.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You can select articles from sound, form regular and unchanged plurals, match is or are to the subject, and identify animals from specific clues.">
    <h3>Final quiz: name it, count it, describe it</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a" data-hint="Dog begins with the consonant sound d." data-fix="I have a dog.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. I have ___ dog.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a">a</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an">an</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="an" data-hint="Owl begins with a vowel sound." data-fix="There is an owl in the tree.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. There is ___ owl in the tree.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a">a</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an">an</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="fish" data-hint="For individual animals of the same kind, the usual plural of fish is fish." data-fix="The aquarium contains exactly two fish of the same kind.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. This aquarium contains exactly two individual animals of the same kind: two ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fish">fish</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fishes">fishes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fishs">fishs</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="are" data-hint="The dogs is a plural subject." data-fix="The dogs are friendly.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. The dogs ___ friendly.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are">are</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is" data-hint="The cat names one animal." data-fix="The cat is black.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. The cat ___ black.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are">are</button></div>
